WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:08.059
Mark Zuckerberg was once on his way to becoming
the richest person in the world.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:15.559
In September 2021, his net worth reached $142
billion, making him the third richest person

00:00:15.559 --> 00:00:16.810
on Earth.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.890
This man gave birth to the social media industry.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:25.890
Yet today, the Facebook founder has seen his
net worth slashed by more than $100 billion…moving

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:30.830
him down to 28th place on the Bloomberg Billionaires
Index.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.190
Zuckerberg’s fall reflects that of his company.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:38.440
At one point, Meta was valued at $1 trillion.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.440
Today, Facebook's parent company has lost
three-quarters of its value.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.559
Its market value is now lower than that of
Home Depot.

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:55.110
On November 9, Meta announced it laid 11,000
people or 13% of its workforce.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:01:01.609
That’s nearly triple the number of employees
Elon Musk let go from Twitter the week before.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:05.390
In a message posted to his company’s website,
Zuckerberg wrote:

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:11.700
“I know this is tough for everyone, and
I’m especially sorry to those impacted.”

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:18.799
Meta has burned billions - spending so furiously
on its virtual world that predictions are

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:24.380
it could eventually cost more than the entire
Apollo moon program…which was more than

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.920
$250 billion adjusted for inflation.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.000
We believe the metaverse will be the successor
to the mobile internet.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.470
We believe in this vision so deeply that we
renamed our whole company after it.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:42.790
Last year, in October 2021, Facebook the company
officially changed its name to Meta to reflect

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.350
a new focus.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:49.719
The metaverse is a vision of the future where
people share virtual worlds through virtual

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:53.310
reality or augmented reality headsets.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:57.850
Quest Pro is the first in a new line of advanced
headsets.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:02.270
In the same way that everyone has a smartphone
today, Zuckerberg is betting they’ll have

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.840
a headset tomorrow.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.560
He’s been intentionally pivoting away from
Facebook.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.780
Facebook’s own research shows it's struggling
to keep young people interested.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:18.090
Facebook’s number of daily active users
dropped at the end of 2021 for the first time.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:23.060
And TikTok has been taking away eyeballs from
Meta’s Instagram while WhatsApp doesn’t

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.060
run ads.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:30.379
It was already a painful year for Meta BEFORE
announcing the large-scale layoffs in November.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:35.700
Meta dropped $232 billion in value in one
day in February.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:41.130
Zuckerberg blamed it partly on Apple’s privacy
changes which gave iPhone owners the choice

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:45.879
of whether they’d allow apps like Facebook
to monitor their online activity.

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:51.240
If people opt out, Facebook receives less
user data, which makes targeting ads more

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.459
difficult, costing the company ad revenue.

00:02:54.459 --> 00:03:02.140
But what’s been really dragging down Meta’s
profit is the ridiculous spending on the metaverse.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:05.340
Spending on the metaverse is absolutely BONKERS.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.340
Hey

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.580
Meta spent $10 billion on the metaverse in
2021 alone.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.590
That’s 10 times what it paid to buy Instagram.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:19.450
$10 billion is just a number I had trouble
processing.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:23.950
I feel sick to my stomach thinking about that
much money being spent.”

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:29.340
John Carmack is an adviser to Meta and the
former chief technology officer at Oculus,

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:32.060
the VR company Facebook acquired.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:37.290
His comments put him at odds with Zuckerberg,
who has put all his eggs in one metaverse

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.760
basket.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:45.041
Zuckerberg is committed to a division of Meta
called Reality Labs - which makes VR and AR

00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:47.750
headsets and software.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:53.920
Reality Labs reportedly has 17,000 employees
- that’s four times the size of Twitter’s

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.900
entire workforce.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.549
Like other tech companies, Meta went on a
hiring spree during the pandemic as everyone

00:04:00.549 --> 00:04:03.220
was locked away at home on their computer.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:10.590
But now, Zuckerberg admits Meta grew too quickly;
the global economy has slowed, inflation has

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:14.280
soared, and investors are nervous about costs.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:20.190
Facebook has weathered storms before - even
scandals related to privacy and misinformation

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.070
didn’t hurt its financial performance.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.699
But this time…it’s different.

00:04:25.699 --> 00:04:30.820
Although tech stocks have been in a slump,
Meta’s problems far outpace both the Nasdaq

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.840
and the S&amp;P 500.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:39.040
November’s job cuts are the most significant
since the company was founded in 2004.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.650
A hiring freeze will be extended until March
2023.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.010
Employees will lose some perks.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:49.979
They already lost free laundry and dry cleaning
earlier in the year.

00:04:49.979 --> 00:04:54.090
Zuckerberg is asking his employees and investors
to trust him.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.720
And his plan for the metaverse.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:05:01.419
In fact, he’s made himself the face of his
company’s push for the metaverse.

00:05:01.419 --> 00:05:07.200
According to the New York Times, some meta
employees refer to metaverse projects as M.M.H.,

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.490
an acronym for “make Mark happy.”

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:16.281
But he wasn’t very happy after he posted
a selfie in Meta’s virtual reality social

00:05:16.281 --> 00:05:22.270
network Horizon Worlds and the world laughed
at him for how ridiculous it looked.

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:27.060
People on Twitter were RUTHLESS, comparing
Horizon Worlds to something outdated from

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.710
decades ago.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:33.960
In response to the mocking, Zuckerberg promised
the graphics would get a lot better and shared

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.620
an improved version three days later.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:41.479
But even Meta’s employees are barely using
its own metaverse app!

00:05:41.479 --> 00:05:47.090
In September, the vice president in charge
of Meta’s metaverse division, Vishal Shah,

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:52.699
wrote in an internal message board obtained
by The Verge: “The simple truth is, if we

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:56.770
don’t love it, how can we expect our users
to love it?”

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:02.150
He said managers would start tracking employees'
use of Horizon Worlds.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:05.600
Nearly all of Zuckerberg’s wealth is tied
up in Meta stock.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:11.669
So he’s betting his entire fortune on the
success of his vision for the future.

00:06:11.669 --> 00:06:15.810
During Meta’s earnings call in October,
Zuckerberg defiantly said:

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.160
“I get that a lot of people might disagree
with this investment.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:24.180
I think people are going to look back on decades
from now and talk about the importance of

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.449
the work that was done here.”

00:06:26.449 --> 00:06:34.960
But for now, as one headline proclaims, its
metaverse dream feels as far away as ever.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:39.730
It remains to be seen whether the metaverse
will transform our lives.

